From: Ahmed Al Hafoudh <alhafoudh@freevision.sk>
Date: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] screen-share: inject remote input into the compositor's seat

screen-share forwards the remote viewer's pointer and keyboard through a
seat of its own, made with weston_seat_init(..., "screen-share") when the
child compositor announces its wl_seat. That is a second wl_seat global,
and a client binds one: Chromium's WaylandConnection keeps the first seat
it sees, which is the libinput seat with the local devices. So every
remote click and key went to a seat nobody listened on.

Inject into the compositor's existing seat instead (the first on
compositor->seat_list; one is made, named "screen-share", only when there
is none at all, and kept until the compositor goes). Remote and local
input then share one cursor and one keyboard focus.

What sharing a seat with local devices takes:

- The seat gets a pointer and a keyboard for as long as the viewer has
  them (weston_seat_init_pointer/_keyboard, released on disconnect).
  libweston counts devices per seat, so local ones are unaffected.
- The child's keymap and modifier mask are not applied: they would replace
  the seat's keymap and overwrite its xkb state. Keys update the state
  themselves (STATE_UPDATE_AUTOMATIC). Both compositors build their keymap
  from the same xkb defaults.
- Enter and leave no longer move focus, and keys and buttons the viewer
  still holds are released when it goes, so nothing stays pressed. Enter's
  position does move the pointer: it is the viewer's first position, and a
  viewer that moves once and clicks sends no motion besides it.
- Positions are converted with weston_coord_global_from_output_point. The
  child's surface is the output's buffer, so its coordinates are output
  pixels, not global ones; they differ once the output is scaled or not at
  0,0.

And a [screen-share] key, input (default true): input=false does not bind
the child's seat at all, and the share is picture only.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Tessaro kiosk policy]

Signed-off-by: Ahmed Al Hafoudh <alhafoudh@freevision.sk>
